{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_http_api_http_api", "label": "HTTP API guide", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L1-L26", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A FastAPI service over the same analysis/ and models/ calls the CLI makes (PYQ-261); additive because cli/app.py was already a mapping from command to a plain function returning a plain dataclass."}, {"id": "docs_http_api_api_key_auth", "label": "X-API-Key authentication (shipped)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L27-L43", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Comparison is constant-time so response timing cannot leak a valid key one byte at a time. Keys come from the environment rather than Settings deliberately: a Settings field can end up in meta.json, a log line or a cache fingerprint, and key values never do. An unconfigured service fails loudly with 500 rather than falling open."}, {"id": "docs_http_api_endpoints", "label": "HTTP endpoint surface (v1)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L45-L57", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Symbols are upper-cased on the way in so /forecast/aapl and /forecast/AAPL are the same bundle."}, {"id": "docs_http_api_status_codes", "label": "HTTP status-code taxonomy (401/404/409/422/500)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L59-L67", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "FeatureSchemaMismatch maps to 409, a conflict rather than a server error: the model is fine, the world moved."}, {"id": "docs_http_api_forecast_endpoint", "label": "GET /forecast/{symbol}", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L69-L78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ForecastResponse is constructed directly from serialize.forecast_to_dict - the same function behind 'pyquant --format json forecast' - so forecast_dates and n_quantile_crossings are present for the same reasons."}, {"id": "docs_http_api_scan_endpoint", "label": "POST /scan", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L80-L90", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Returns 200 even when individual symbols fail; each row carries status ok/not_trained/error. Same scan_row_to_dict implementation as the CLI so signal and band_width_pct cannot drift between front-ends."}, {"id": "docs_http_api_train_endpoint", "label": "POST /train and GET /train/{job_id}", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L92-L110", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Training takes minutes so POST /train returns 202 immediately; status moves queued -> running -> succeeded|failed."}, {"id": "docs_http_api_bundle_cache_eviction", "label": "Bundle-cache eviction after a successful train job", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L108-L110", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Without evicting the retrained bundle, a cached copy from before the run would keep serving the old weights to the next /forecast or /explain."}, {"id": "docs_http_api_concurrency_model", "label": "Shipped concurrency model", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L112-L130", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Both mechanisms come from measured behaviour rather than assumption: a cold call is ~98% vendor fetch and panel build (~65 s) and the forward pass is under a second either way, so optimising the model path would have been optimising 2% of the wall clock."}, {"id": "docs_http_api_lru_bundle_cache", "label": "LRU cache of 8 loaded bundles (shipped)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L116-L119", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Loading is real file I/O plus checkpoint deserialisation; the load happens outside the cache lock so loading one bundle does not block requests for bundles already resident."}, {"id": "docs_http_api_per_bundle_lock", "label": "One lock per bundle (shipped)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L121-L126", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "predict() is unsafe concurrently on one model instance because pytorch-forecasting spins up an internal Lightning Trainer per call and mutates model state. Different bundles proceed in parallel; the cost is low because torch already uses multiple cores within a call."}, {"id": "docs_http_api_v1_limits", "label": "What API v1 deliberately does not do", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L132-L148", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "In-process job registry, per-process bundle cache, local-filesystem bundles, no rate limiting. These are documented triggers to graduate rather than defects to file: cheap to live with for a single instance and wrong to pretend away for more than one."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_http_api_http_api", "target": "docs_api_design_design_note", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L9-L11", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_http_api_lru_bundle_cache", "target": "docs_api_design_bundle_lru_cache", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L116-L119", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_http_api_per_bundle_lock", "target": "docs_api_design_per_bundle_lock", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L121-L126", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_http_api_api_key_auth", "target": "docs_api_design_api_key_auth", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L27-L43", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_http_api_train_endpoint", "target": "docs_api_design_background_jobs", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L92-L110", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_http_api_v1_limits", "target": "docs_api_design_queue_graduation_triggers", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L132-L148", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_http_api_v1_limits", "target": "docs_api_design_bundle_storage", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L141-L143", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_http_api_v1_limits", "target": "docs_api_design_rate_limiting", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L144-L146", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_http_api_concurrency_model", "target": "docs_api_design_latency_profile", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L127-L130", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_http_api_concurrency_model", "target": "docs_http_api_lru_bundle_cache", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L112-L119", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_http_api_concurrency_model", "target": "docs_http_api_per_bundle_lock", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L121-L126", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_http_api_bundle_cache_eviction", "target": "docs_http_api_lru_bundle_cache", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L108-L110", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_http_api_bundle_cache_eviction", "target": "docs_http_api_train_endpoint", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L108-L110", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_http_api_forecast_endpoint", "target": "docs_cli_json_output", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L75-L78", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_http_api_scan_endpoint", "target": "docs_cli_scan", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L86-L89", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_http_api_forecast_endpoint", "target": "docs_cli_forecast", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L69-L78", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_http_api_status_codes", "target": "docs_cli_exit_codes", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "source_location": "L59-L67", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_http_api_api_key_auth", "target": "docs_api_configuration_secrets_rule", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/http-api.md", "sour